# Content is deliberately NOT under version control. It is all binary .uasset/
# .umap, so every editor save shows up as an opaque "Bin X -> Y bytes" change
# that cannot be reviewed, merged, or reverted meaningfully - and much of the
# churn isn't design work at all: the test level balloons because ISM
# components serialize their runtime instances into the .umap on every save
# after a GenerateRandom() stress run, and assets like Music_controller
# rewrite themselves on save with no real diff. Those two were excluded
# individually first; this replaces both with the whole folder.
#
# The cost, stated plainly: a fresh clone gives the C++ project without its
# level, HUD widgets, blueprints, meshes or materials, i.e. it will not run
# as-is. Content lives only on disk here - back it up separately.
Content/